request.description:
Initiates Google SSO login. Generates a state UUID and nonce, stores them in stateStore (TTL 10 min), and returns the Google OAuth2 authorization URL.

Response: { authUrl: 'https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth?...', state: '<uuid>' }

The client should redirect the user's browser to authUrl. Google will redirect back to /iam/sso/google/callback with code and state.

Initiates SSO login for a state-configured OIDC provider. Provider name must be prefixed with 'state_' followed by the state code (e.g. state_karnataka, state_maharashtra).

The state code is looked up in STATE_SSO_PROVIDERS config. Returns 400 if the state provider is not configured.

Response: { authUrl: '<state_auth_endpoint>?...', state: '<uuid>' }
